---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'; import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro'; import { capabilities } from '../data/site';
const working = ['Gerber AccuMark / 2D workflow','Pattern development from sketch, specification, block or reference','Pattern modification and buyer-comment interpretation','Production size-set grading','Digital and manual pattern checking','Basic marker making and solid-fabric consumption','Fit / PP / size-set sample exposure','DXF to Gerber workflow','Buyer-facing email and technical follow-up'];
const learning = ['Systematic seam construction and allowance logic','Fabric behaviour across pattern, sewing and fit','Comprehensive fit diagnosis and drag-line analysis','Complex clean-finish construction','Advanced grading theory','Advanced CLO 3D','Direct production-line adjustment','Leadership and technical-management evidence'];
---
<Base title="Expertise" description="An evidence-led view of Shorif Ahmmed’s current garment pattern-making capabilities, CLO 3D validation practice and active technical development areas.">
  <section class="page-hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">Expertise</p><h1>Practical capability, with the <em>edges clearly marked.</em></h1><p class="lead narrow">A credible technical profile should distinguish demonstrated practice from developing knowledge. This page does exactly that.</p></section>
  <section class="shell section-space"><SectionHead eyebrow="Current practice" title="Where I contribute today." /><div class="capability-grid">{capabilities.map(x => <article><span>{x.n}</span><h3>{x.title}</h3><p>{x.body}</p></article>)}</div><div class="skill-panel"><h3>Working capabilities</h3><ul class="check-list">{working.map(x => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul></div></section>

  <section class="dark-section"><div class="shell section-space split"><SectionHead eyebrow="CLO 3D" title="3D as a pattern decision checkpoint—not only a buyer visualization tool." /><div class="prose"><p>In many apparel workflows, CLO 3D is used heavily for buyer visualization and presentation. My current use is more pattern-focused.</p><p>I draft or prepare the pattern, bring it into CLO 3D, dress it on an avatar and inspect how the style is likely to read before the physical sample is finalized. When I receive a new design, tech pack or inspiration image, I use the simulation to understand the intended shape, proportion and visible pattern behaviour.</p><p>The purpose is not to claim that 3D replaces the sample. It is an additional checking layer before I commit to the pattern decision and release it for the next stage. My CLO 3D capability is still developing, so I present this as a practical validation workflow rather than advanced virtual-product expertise.</p><a class="button light-button" href="/projects/clo-3d-pattern-validation">View the CLO 3D study →</a></div></div></section>

  <section id="learning" class="learning-band"><div class="shell"><SectionHead eyebrow="Active development" title="The next layer of technical depth." body="These subjects are part of a deliberate mastery roadmap. They are not presented as advanced expertise." /><ol class="learning-list">{learning.map((x,i) => <li><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span>{x}</li>)}</ol></div></section>
  <section class="shell section-space split"><SectionHead eyebrow="Tools" title="Technology supports the judgment." /><div class="prose"><h3>Primary</h3><p>Gerber AccuMark / PDS for 2D pattern work, modification, grading and checking.</p><h3>Developing</h3><p>CLO 3D for pattern validation, style interpretation and pre-sample checking; Optitex exploration; spreadsheets for measurement and structured evidence.</p><h3>AI & workflow systems</h3><p>Researching and building AI-assisted retrieval, documentation, agent and workflow concepts that reduce repetitive work while keeping pattern and garment decisions accountable to human technical judgment.</p></div></section>
</Base>
